{
  "slug": "neutrally",
  "name": "Neutrally",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Persistent cross-session memory for Claude Code. Neutrally auto-injects your project context, decisions, and tech stack at session start so Claude already knows who you are and what you're building. Conversations are captured every 5 minutes and survive /compact, crashes, and session restarts. Memory works across Claude Code, VS Code, Cursor, and neutrally.app.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill**, **5 commands**, **3 hooks** and **1 MCP server**.\n\n- **Skills** (1): `memory-injection` (Use when working in any Claude Code session — governs how to use Neutrally persistent memory naturally and…)\n- **Commands** (5): `context` (Show what Neutrally memory context is currently active for this session), `forget` (Remove a specific memory item from Neutrally), `save` (Manually save a decision, convention, or important note to Neutrally memory), `search` (Search your Neutrally memory for past decisions, conversations, or context), `setup` (Connect Neutrally persistent memory to Claude Code)\n- **Hooks** (3): `SessionStart`, `UserPromptSubmit`, `PostToolUse`\n- **MCP servers** (1): `neutrally`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install neutrally@claude-community` from `Neutrally-app/neutrally-claude-plugin`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 1,
    "hook": 3,
    "command": 5,
    "mcp": 1
  },
